<%# locals: (bank_rows: [], checked_account_id: :unspecified, account_last4s: {}) %>
<%# Allocation dialog BANK SOURCE rows (round 21 T8): the "No bank
    (unassigned)" radio + one row per on-plan account, extracted from
    _allocation_dialog.html.erb so the list can refresh IN PLACE. The
    dialog body renders once at page load; render_flow_json ships this
    fragment (chrome.allocation_bank_rows) after an in-place account
    add/remove/update and #inPlaceSubmit swaps it into every allocation
    dialog (allocation:new and allocation:<id>).
    The radio NAME (plan_allocation[account_id]) is unchanged, so the
    save contract (field names/order) and the #checkAccountRadio checked
    rules in _allocation_dialog.html.erb stay intact across a swap.
    Three-state checked semantics:
      - :unspecified (the render_flow_json fragment, which serves ALL
        allocation dialogs at once and cannot encode per-allocation
        state): NO radio is checked; #inPlaceSubmit re-checks the radio
        each dialog's form held before the swap (a closed dialog keeps
        its form in the DOM, so the live checked state is readable).
      - nil (the dialog's page-load render for an unassigned allocation):
        the "No bank (unassigned)" row is checked.
      - an account id (the dialog's page-load render for an assigned
        allocation): that account's row is checked.
    i18n keys are the dialog's explicit keys (a partial's lazy scope is
    its own name, so t(".source_bank_unassigned") would miss here). %>
<%# Round 22 (N1/N6/N7): each bank row appends the masked ****last4
    (account_last4s — plain 4 digits from PaycheckFlowPlanner, nil rows
    render nothing); the avatar is the plan-flow logo (keyword-resolved
    via plan_flow_avatar_url, N6) OVERLAYED on the always-rendered letter
    chip (onerror removes a dead <img> so a broken asset degrades to the
    chip); the root div is the LOCKED scroll window (max-h-64
    overflow-y-auto — never overflow-auto: #showAllocationForm
    querySelectors the dialog's .overflow-auto and must not scroll this
    list). The root stays the single fragment element. %>
<% assigning = checked_account_id != :unspecified %>
<%# Round 26 R4 (item 6): the radios carry additive data attrs for the
    bank-source trigger sync (#applyBankSelection in plan_flow_controller.js
    mirrors the checked row into the form's hidden
    plan_allocation[account_id] input + the labeled-row trigger):
    data-bank-name / data-bank-last4 on the account radios, data-bank-none
    on the unassigned radio, and data-bank-row-chip on the avatar chip the
    trigger clones. Additive only — the in-place swap (render_flow_json
    chrome.allocation_bank_rows) re-renders this same partial, so the
    swapped rows carry the same attrs. %>
<div data-flow-chrome="allocation-bank-rows" class="max-h-64 overflow-y-auto space-y-1 overscroll-contain">
  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1.5 cursor-pointer has-[:checked]:bg-surface-inset">
    <input type="radio" name="plan_allocation[account_id]" value="" class="sr-only" data-bank-none="true"
           <%= "checked" if assigning && checked_account_id.nil? %>>
    <span class="h-8 w-8 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-subdued flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-medium text-secondary"
          data-bank-row-chip>?</span>
    <span class="text-sm text-secondary"><%= t("plan_flows.allocation_dialog.source_bank_unassigned") %></span>
  </label>
  <% bank_rows.each do |account| %>
    <label class="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1.5 cursor-pointer has-[:checked]:bg-surface-inset">
      <input type="radio" name="plan_allocation[account_id]" value="<%= account.id %>" class="sr-only"
             data-bank-name="<%= account.name %>"
             data-bank-last4="<%= account_last4s[account.id] %>"
             <%= "checked" if assigning && checked_account_id.to_s == account.id.to_s %>>
      <%# Same avatar the bank config dialog uses (round 20d): the
          plan-flow logo when present, else the neutral letter chip.
          Round 22 (N6): the letter chip is ALWAYS rendered behind and
          the logo overlays it (onerror removes a dead <img> so a broken
          asset degrades to the chip, never a broken-image glyph). %>
      <span class="h-8 w-8 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full overflow-hidden bg-subdued flex items-center justify-center relative"
            data-bank-row-chip>
        <span class="text-sm font-medium text-secondary"><%= (account.name.to_s.strip.first || "?").upcase %></span>
        <% if account.plan_flow_avatar_url.present? %>
          <img src="<%= account.plan_flow_avatar_url %>" alt="" class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover" onerror="this.remove()">
        <% end %>
      </span>
      <span class="text-sm text-primary truncate"><%= account.name %></span>
      <%# Round 22 (N1): the masked last 4, modal-style ****NNNN (nil for
          every account without a plaid_accounts.mask — never fabricated). %>
      <% if (last4 = account_last4s[account.id]) %>
        <span class="text-xs text-secondary tabular-nums">****<%= last4 %></span>
      <% end %>
    </label>
  <% end %>
  <% if bank_rows.empty? %>
    <p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= t("plan_flows.allocation_dialog.empty_bank_rows") %></p>
  <% end %>
</div>
